From: Longwei Yang <19267252+Longwei-Yang@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:27:20 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 10/17] Safarium: video full screen on YouTube's own button

YouTube's full-screen button and its "f" key put the whole page (<html>)
in full screen and enlarge the player with their own CSS, so the zoom
started and ended at the whole page instead of the video.

- Blink anchors the reported full-screen rect on the largest video inside
  the full-screen element when that element isn't a video itself.
- Entering waits (up to 0.6 s) until a video fills the full-screen window
  before zooming, so the video grows rather than a miniature of the page.
- Leaving hands back once a video is at that anchor again (or the videos
  have stopped moving), instead of comparing with rects measured after the
  site had already enlarged its player.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
